The '''Mercedes-AMG One''' (R50, previously known as '''Project One''') is a limited-production [[plug-in hybrid|plug-in]] [[dual hybrid]] [[sports car]] manufactured by [[Mercedes-AMG]], featuring [[Formula One]]–derived technology.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://media.daimler.com/marsMediaSite/en/instance/ko.xhtml?oid=29206687&ls=L2VuL2luc3RhbmNlL2tvLnhodG1sP29pZD00ODM2MjU4JnJlbElkPTYwODI5JmZyb21PaWQ9NDgzNjI1OCZib3JkZXJzPXRydWUmcmVzdWx0SW5mb1R5cGVJZD00MDYyNiZ2aWV3VHlwZT10aHVtYnM!&rs=0|title = World première of the Mercedes-AMG Project ONE show car: Mercedes-AMG brings Formula 1 technology to the road}}</ref><ref name=Mercedes1>{{cite web|title=Mercedes-AMG Project ONE: Announcement of the hypercar| url=https://www.mercedes-benz.com/en/mercedes-benz/vehicles/announcement-mercedes-amg-project-one/|work=[[Mercedes-AMG]]|accessdate=2017-03-15|date=2017-03-16}}</ref> The Project One concept car was unveiled at the [[International Motor Show Germany#2017|2017 International Motor Show Germany]] by then three-time [[Formula One World Drivers' Champion]] and [[Mercedes-Benz in Formula One|Mercedes]] driver [[Lewis Hamilton]] and head of [[Mercedes-Benz]], [[Dieter Zetsche]].<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://autoweek.com/article/supercars/three-time-world-champion-lewis-hamiltons-take-project-one|title=Here's Lewis Hamilton's take on the Mercedes-AMG Project One|work=Autoweek|access-date=2018-04-23}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.motor1.com/news/180098/mercedes-project-one-aston-valkyrie/|title=HyperFight: Mercedes-AMG Project One vs. Aston Martin Valkyrie|last=Alaniz|first=Anthony|date=2017-09-17|work=Motor1.com|access-date=2018-04-23|language=en}}</ref>

The production version of the AMG One was unveiled on 1 June 2022 and production began in August.<ref name=":6">{{Cite web |title=Mercedes-AMG One Production Starts, Assembly Is Done By Hand |url=https://www.motor1.com/news/603438/mercedes-amg-one-production-start/ |access-date=2022-08-10 |website=Motor1.com |language=en}}</ref>

== Development ==
Mercedes-AMG unveiled the concept version of the One in 2017, the Project One with nearly identical specifications to the production version from 2022. Claimed that the production One will be evaluated on their performance, durability, and ability in Mercedes-Benz's proving grounds and on racing circuits. Development of the AMG One took place at [[Mercedes-AMG]], in [[Affalterbach]], Germany. Head of Mercedes-AMG, [[Tobias Moers]] described that  when "the time is right", Lewis Hamilton, who has worked on the development of the car will join the team of development drivers testing prototypes of the car.<ref name=":1">{{Cite web|url=https://www.autocar.co.uk/car-news/mercedes-amg-hypercar|title=2018 Mercedes-AMG Project One commences on track testing {{!}} Autocar|website=www.autocar.co.uk|language=en|access-date=2017-04-21}}</ref>

== Production ==
The production version of the AMG One unveiled on 1 June 2022. Production was expected to begin in late 2022 and planned to be limited for 275 units at a price of US$2.72 million per unit, all of which had been already sold. Mercedes-AMG received orders more than four times of the planned production number, but they refused to increase the production limit, in order to maintain exclusivity of the car.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Zhang |first=Benjamin |date=2017-09-11 |title=Here's our first look at Mercedes' new $2.7 million hypercar |work=Business Insider |url=http://www.businessinsider.com/frankfurt-motor-show-mercedes-amg-project-one-hybrid-hypercar-2017-9 |access-date=2018-04-23}}</ref> Production of the AMG One began in August 2022, all 275 cars were set to be hand built by Mercedes-AMG, with deliveries to begin in late 2022.<ref name=":6" /> The first car was delivered on 16 January 2023, which had an exclusive paint job inspired by the livery of the [[Mercedes W12|F1 W12 E Performance]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Mercedes-AMG One Deliveries Start: See The Very First Car |url=https://www.motor1.com/news/631246/mercedes-amg-deliveries-start/ |access-date=2023-01-17 |website=Motor1.com |language=en}}</ref>

== Design ==

=== Exterior features ===
[[File:Mercedes-AMG One IAA 2021 1X7A0112.jpg|thumb|Rear view|left]]
The exterior of the car is designed primarily for better aerodynamics. Notable aerodynamic features include; moveable slats which were specifically developed for the front wheelhouses, two-part extendable rear wing with [[Drag reduction system|DRS]] system and active flaps on the front diffuser which were adjustable to suit the driver chosen driving program. Additionally, large front air inlets, roof-mounted air intake, large aerodynamic fin extending down the back half of the car and aerodynamically optimized wheels to aid generate more downforce in order to carry the maximum speed at highspeed corners.<ref name=":5" />

=== Powertrain ===
The powertrain of the Mercedes-AMG One is rated at {{convert|782|kW|PS hp|abbr=on}} through a [[Hybrid vehicle drivetrain|hybrid drivetrain]] that shares many features with modern F1 cars. The car has an internal combustion engine and four electric motors.

==== Internal combustion engine ====
[[File:2016 Mercedes PU106 Hybrid Power Unit including battery (49254448503).jpg|thumb|2016 Mercedes PU106 Hybrid Power Unit including battery]]

The car on which the engine and design of the One is based on is the [[Mercedes F1 W06 Hybrid|Mercedes-AMG F1 W06]], as confirmed by Mercedes-AMG board member [[Ola Källenius]]. The Mercedes-AMG One utilises a modified version of the [[Mercedes V6 Hybrid Formula One engine|Mercedes-Benz PU106B Hybrid]] engine, a 1.6-litre [[Turbocharger|turbocharged]] 90-degree V6 engine.<ref name=":0">{{Cite news|url=https://www.motorauthority.com/news/1121083_watch-mercedes-benz-amg-s-one-hit-the-hockenheimring-racetrack|title=Watch Mercedes-Benz AMG's One hit the Hockenheimring racetrack|work=Motor Authority|access-date=2022-07-19|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.carwow.co.uk/mercedes/news/3950/mercedes-amg-project-one-price-specs-and-release-date#gref|title=New Mercedes-AMG One revealed: price, specs and release date|website=Carwow|access-date=2022-07-19}}</ref> Modifications were done to the engine as to make comply with the idle RPM and redline regulations. Tobias Moers, claimed that the engine would be at 1,280 rpm at idle, and 11,000 rpm at its redline limit.<ref name="TopGear1">{{cite web|url=https://www.topgear.com/car-news/geneva-motor-show/mercedes-amg-project-one-hypercar-will-cost-eu2275m|title=The Mercedes-AMG Project One hypercar will cost €2.275m|date=2017-03-07|author=Jack Rix|work=[[Top Gear (magazine)|Top Gear]]|accessdate=2017-03-17}}</ref> However, the engine would only last for {{convert|50,000|km|mi|-3|abbr=on}} and the owners will have to return their cars for an engine refurbishment.<ref name="motor_au1">{{cite web|url=http://www.motoring.com.au/amg-hypercar-engine-only-good-for-50000km-106343/|title=AMG hypercar engine only good for 50,000km|date=2017-03-10|author=Feann Torr|work=motoring.com.au|accessdate=2017-03-15|url-status=dead|archiveurl=https://archive.today/20170421093407/http://www.motoring.com.au/amg-hypercar-engine-only-good-for-50000km-106343/|archivedate=2017-04-21}}</ref> The ICE produces {{convert|422|kW|PS hp|abbr=on|0}}, torque figures were claimed to be unmeasurable due to the complex drivetrain. Top speed of this car is limited at 219&nbsp;mph (352&nbsp;km/h).<ref name=":2">{{Cite news|url=https://carbuzz.com/news/the-mercedes-amg-project-one-hypercar-will-have-1-020-hp|title=The Mercedes-AMG Project One Hypercar Will Have 1,020 HP|last=Traugott|first=Jay|date=2017-04-24|work=CarBuzz|access-date=2018-04-23|language=en-us}}</ref>

==== Electric motors ====
The internal combustion engine works in conjunction with four electric motors: a {{convert|120|kW|PS hp|0|abbr=on}} motor generator unit-kinetic ([[MGU-K]]) coupled to the crankshaft, a {{convert|90|kW|PS hp|0|abbr=on}} motor generator unit-heat ([[MGU-H]]) coupled to the turbocharger, and two {{convert|120|kW|PS hp|0|abbr=on}} electric motors at the front axle.<ref name=":3">{{Cite news|url=https://www.caranddriver.com/news/mercedes-amg-project-one-photos-and-info-news|title=Mercedes-AMG Project One Photos and Info {{!}} News {{!}} Car and Driver|last=Csere|first=Csaba|date=2017-09-17|work=Car and Driver|access-date=2018-04-23|language=en}}</ref> The MGU-K and MGU-H are Formula One-style motors responsible for recovering energy and improving efficiency during the operation of the car.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/championship/inside-f1/understanding-f1-racing/Energy_Recovery_Systems.html|title=Power unit and ERS|website=Formula1.com|language=en|access-date=2018-04-23}}</ref> More specifically, the MGU-K serves to generate electricity during braking, while the MGU-H serves to eliminate [[Turbocharger#Turbocharger lag|turbo lag]] in order to improve throttle response by keeping the turbine spinning at lower engine speeds and also to recover waste energy from the exhaust.<ref name=":3" /> The final two electric motors driving the front wheels make up for an all-wheel drive drivetrain, the sum of these four electric motors contribute {{convert|360|kW|PS hp|0|abbr=on}} 
of effective power to the total power output figure of the AMG One.<ref name=":2" />

=== Transmission ===
The AMG One features a 7-speed single-clutch [[automated manual transmission]] with 4-disc carbon racing clutch (similar to the type of transmission used in modern F1 cars), and delivers the bulk of the engine power and torque to the rear wheels. The use of a single-clutch over a [[dual-clutch transmission]] was due to engineers wanting to keep the car light and concerns over the dual-clutch's ability to handle the high-revving ICE.<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://www.motortrend.com/news/revealed-2019-mercedes-amg-project-one-powertrain/|title=Revealed: 2019 Mercedes-AMG Project One Powertrain - Motor Trend|last=MacKenzie|first=Angus|date=2017-05-30|work=Motor Trend|access-date=2018-04-23|language=en-US}}</ref><ref name=":5">{{Cite web |title=Mercedes-AMG ONE |url=https://www.mercedes-amg.com/en/vehicles/amg-one/hypercar.html |access-date=2022-07-18 |website=www.mercedes-amg.com |language=en}}</ref>

=== Suspension and wheels ===
The car contains a five-link aluminium [[Coilover|coil-over]] suspension setup with two transverse adjustable [[Push-rod suspension|push-rod]] spring struts, including adaptive damping adjustments. Rear axle links are shaped for better aerodynamics. It also features the hydraulic AMG carbon-fibre ceramic high-performance composite brake system, with 398 x 38&nbsp;mm front composite brake discs, ventilated with 6-piston aluminium fixed callipers. 380 x 34&nbsp;mm rear composite brake discs, ventilated with 4-piston aluminium fixed callipers. Additionally electric parking brake, [[Anti-lock braking system|ABS]], brake assist and 3-stage ESP were also offered for the car.

The AMG One also has unique 10-spoke forged [[aluminium|aluminium alloy]] wheels emerged with NACA [[Carbon fiber reinforced polymer|carbon fibre]] openings for brake cooling and increase downforce. Also, with diameters of 19 inches at the front and 20 inches at the rear with F1-styled centre-lock wheel nuts. The tyres are semi-slick [[Michelin]] Pilot Sport Cup 2Rs with [[Tire code|codes]] of 285/35 ZR 19 for the front and 335/30 ZR 20 for the rear. The brakes are ventilated [[Ceramic matrix composite|carbon-ceramic]] discs.<ref name=":5" />

=== Interior features ===
[[File:Mercedes-AMG Project One, IAA 2017, Frankfurt (1Y7A3441).jpg|thumb|Interior]]
The interior is mostly minimalist and driver-focused, continuing the F1 theme of the AMG One. This includes [[Mercedes-AMG|AMG Motorsport]] bucket seats, integrated into the carbon monocoque, a F1-style steering wheel with knobs for driving programs including; DRS, overtake etc. Paddle shifters and a driver-oriented central [[In-car entertainment|infotainment screen]] were also featured in the car. There are some traditional luxury features in the interior, notably the [[napa leather]] and hand stitching on the bucket seats.<ref name=":4">{{Cite web|url=https://www.mercedes-amg.com/en/driving-performance/future-performance/mercedes-amg-project-one.html|title=Mercedes-AMG Project ONE Show car.|website=www.mercedes-amg.com|language=de|access-date=2018-04-23}}</ref><ref name=":5" />

=== Chassis ===
[[File:Mercedes-AMG_Project_One,_IAA_2017,_Frankfurt_(1Y7A2932).jpg|alt=Mercedes-AMG Project One, IAA 2017, Frankfurt (1Y7A2932)|thumb|F1 inspired exhaust pipes]]
The body is made entirely out of carbon fiber in line with its F1 counterpart, resulting in a final [[kerb weight]] of {{convert|1695|kg|lbs|0|abbr=on}}.<ref name=":0" /><ref name=":1" /> The car also features the F1 inspired exhaust tailpipe with a large round main outlet and two smaller outlets.
{{clear}}

== Performance ==
[[File:Mercedes-AMG_One_IAA_2021_1X7A0108.jpg|alt=Mercedes-AMG One IAA 2021 1X7A0108|thumb|AMG ONE in Strat 2 mode]]
The One has six different drive modes, including:
* "Race safe" mode; which features a hybrid driving mode with an all-electric start up. The ICE is switched at higher speeds.
* "Race" mode is also a hybrid driving mode with a special energy recovery strategy. Also, with a continuous combustion engine run and battery charging.
* "EV" mode is an all-electric driving mode.
* "Race plus" mode features active aerodynamics; front diffuser flaps folds up to shape, rear wing is fully extended, louvres (front fender vents) open up, lower the car by 37&nbsp;mm in front and 30&nbsp;mm in rear, chassis tuning and special performance management.
* "Strat 2" mode, which features all "Race Plus" changes and additionally with firmer suspension tuning and full electric power from all electric motors. This is a similar driving mode as used in F1 cars during qualifying sessions. Furthermore, the driver can save their personal favourite settings under the "individual" mode.

In "Race plus" and "Strat 2" modes, the total vehicle downforce is increased by up to five times when compared to other drive modes. The AMG One also features F1's [[Drag reduction system|Drag Reduction System]] (DRS). Reducing the vehicle's overall downforce by 20 percent from lowering the rear wing flaps and closing the front louvers to increase straight line speed. DRS can be turned off by manually and automatically from applying brakes.<ref>{{Cite web |title=The new Mercedes-AMG ONE: Formula 1 technology for the road |url=https://group-media.mercedes-benz.com/marsMediaSite/en/instance/ko/The-new-Mercedes-AMG-ONE-Formula-1-technology-for-the-road.xhtml?oid=53396743 |access-date=2022-07-22 |website=marsMediaSite |language=en}}</ref>

Official performance and standstill acceleration times claimed by Mercedes-AMG:
*Top speed: {{cvt|352|kph|mph|0|abbr=on}}
*0-{{cvt|100|kph|mph|0|abbr=on}}: 2.9 seconds
*0-{{cvt|200|kph|mph|0|abbr=on}}: 7.0 seconds
*0-{{cvt|300|kph|mph|0|abbr=on}}: 15.6 seconds

===Lap records===
In November 2022, the AMG One set a lap time of 6:35.183 minutes around the [[Nürburgring|Nürburgring Nordschleife]] 12.944 mile (20.832&nbsp;km) course. Driven by [[Maro Engel]], it became the [[List of Nürburgring Nordschleife lap times|fastest road-legal production car around the track]], beating the previous record by over 13 seconds, held by the [[Mercedes-AMG GT|Mercedes-AMG GT Black Series]]. Engel revealed the track was not in ideal conditions, as some parts of the track were still on damp conditions and he had to lift throttle at those particular corners. Mercedes-AMG claimed the car could have easily done a sub 6:30 minute lap time, if the track was in ideal conditions.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2022-11-10 |title=The Mercedes-AMG One Just Set an Absurd Nürburgring Record |url=https://www.caranddriver.com/news/a41923420/mercedes-amg-one-nurburgring-record/ |access-date=2023-01-17 |website=Car and Driver |language=en-us}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Mercedes-AMG One breaks Nurburgring lap record |url=https://www.autoexpress.co.uk/mercedes/104697/mercedes-amg-one-breaks-nurburgring-lap-record |access-date=2023-01-17 |website=Auto Express |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2022-11-10 |title=The Mercedes-AMG One is the fastest ever production car around the Nürburgring |url=https://www.topgear.com/car-news/supercars/mercedes-amg-one-fastest-ever-production-car-around-nurburgring |access-date=2023-01-17 |website=Top Gear |language=en}}</ref>

Mercedes-AMG later tested this claim and, in September 2024, set another laptime in optimal track conditions with a time of 6:29.09 minutes, beating its own record by another 6 seconds. This makes the AMG One the first road-legal production car to set a sub-6:30 minute lap time around the [[Nürburgring|Nürburgring Nordschleife]] 12.944 mile (20.832 km) course.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Pattni |first=Vijay |date=2024-10-02 |title=The Mercedes-AMG One has broken its own Nürburgring record by six seconds |url=https://www.topgear.com/car-news/supercars/mercedes-amg-one-has-broken-its-own-nurburgring-record-six-seconds |website=TopGear}}</ref>

Following the 2022 Nürburgring lap record, Mercedes-AMG revealed that the AMG One has set new lap records around the Nürburgring Grand Prix circuit, [[Hockenheimring]], and [[Red Bull Ring]], setting lap times of 1:56.096 minutes, 1:38.563 minutes and 1:26.846 minutes respectively.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Mercedes-AMG highlights the One hypercar's track records |url=https://uk.motor1.com/news/624704/mercede-amg-one-track-records-video/ |access-date=2023-01-17 |website=Motor1.com |language=en-gb}}</ref> In April 2023, the AMG One was claimed to have set another production car lap record with a time of 1:43.902 minutes around the [[Monza Circuit]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Mercedes-AMG One breaks production car record at Monza |url=https://www.evo.co.uk/mercedes/18211/mercedes-amg-one-breaks-production-car-record-at-monza |website=evo |access-date=5 April 2023 |language=en}}</ref>
{{clear}}

